  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">#cocreateMYCITY Durban 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CoCreateMyCity is an initiative in South Africa that aims to encourage collaboration between citizens, government, and the private sector in order to improve urban areas. The CoCreateMyCity initiative in Durban can contribute to local private sector development by creating new business opportunities, supporting SMEs, improving the local economy, and fostering innovation and creativity in the water and sanitation sector. By involving a range of local as well as Dutch stakeholders in the process, the initiative can help to build strong and resilient communities that are well positioned for a future-proof water sector.The CoCreateMyCity initiative contributes to other initiatives such as the Wavemakers program possibly by involving the Orange Corners program, it gives the Dutch Risk Reduction mission a platform to share their findings, and the event also functions as a good follow-up for the Game Changer Challenge South Africa where the PSDTK also invested in through project PSS23ZA01.</narrative>
  </description>
